WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.958
Containers can simplify application dependencies,

00:00:01.958 --> 00:00:05.301
but they do not remove host GPU driver requirements.

00:00:05.301 --> 00:00:10.131
The host still needs the right driver, kernel modules, device nodes, and permissions.

00:00:10.131 --> 00:00:14.960
The container runtime then exposes GPU devices and compatible libraries into the container.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:19.418
If the host stack is broken, the container cannot magically repair it.

00:00:19.418 --> 00:00:20.533
For NVIDIA systems,

00:00:20.533 --> 00:00:24.991
the NVIDIA Container Toolkit is commonly used at a high level to

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:26.848
make GPUs available to containers.

00:00:26.848 --> 00:00:30.935
ROCm container workflows have their own considerations around devices, groups, libraries,

00:00:30.935 --> 00:00:32.050
and supported images.

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:33.164
In both cases,

00:00:33.164 --> 00:00:37.622
the container image must be compatible with the host driver and the

00:00:37.622 --> 00:00:39.851
runtime expectations of the AI application.

00:00:39.851 --> 00:00:43.938
Container failures often come from missing runtime configuration, missing device access,

00:00:43.938 --> 00:00:46.538
permissions, incorrect image selection, or version mismatch.

00:00:46.538 --> 00:00:50.996
A container might run successfully but still use the CPU if the

00:00:50.996 --> 00:00:53.225
application cannot see the GPU libraries.

00:00:53.225 --> 00:00:57.312
Validation should happen inside the container, not only on the host.

00:00:57.312 --> 00:01:02.513
The question is whether the workload sees and uses acceleration where it actually runs.

00:01:02.513 --> 00:01:06.600
Good container practice includes documenting the host driver, container runtime settings,

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:09.943
image tags, environment variables, mounted devices, and validation output.

00:01:09.943 --> 00:01:12.172
Pin known-good images for stable systems.

00:01:12.172 --> 00:01:12.915
Update deliberately.

00:01:12.915 --> 00:01:15.516
Containers make AI applications easier to package,

00:01:15.516 --> 00:01:20.345
but GPU access remains a contract between host driver, runtime configuration, image contents,

00:01:20.345 --> 00:01:21.460
and application code.
